course: dictionary
lesson: 15595
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show which meaning the writer wants. «Sam was tagged, so he had to chase everyone.» The clue is the chasing, so tagged means touched in a game of tag.
explain: «The new coat was tagged with a price.» A label is fixed to the coat, so tagged means it had a label or tag attached. Always ask: what is the sentence about? Then pick the meaning that fits.
explain: Tagged can also mean marked online with a name, or fitted with a small device so scientists can follow an animal. Tagged along means went with someone, often without being invited.
fact: Tagged is the past form of the verb tag, and it can also be an adjective.
fact: Tagged means caught by being touched in the game of tag, also called tig or it.
fact: Tagged means having a label or tag fixed to it.
fact: Tagged means marked online with a name, so that a person is linked to a photo or post.
fact: Tagged along means went with someone, often without being invited.
exercise: «Sam was tagged, so he had to chase everyone.» What does tagged mean here? | *Touched in the game of tag, so he is now it | Wet from the rain | Hidden behind a big tree | Given a prize for winning the race
exercise: «The new coat was tagged with a price.» What does tagged mean here? | Was folded neatly in a box | Was torn at the sleeve | Was cleaned at the shop | *Had a label fixed to it
exercise: Ruby says, «Please ask before you tag me in a photo.» What does tag mean here? | Hit me gently on the arm | Draw a picture of me | *Mark a photo online with my name | Take a photo of me with a camera
test: «Scientists tagged the turtles so they could track where they swam.» What does tagged mean here? | Took them home as pets | Painted them bright colours | Fed them special food | *Fixed a small device to them so they can be followed
test: «Mia tagged along with her big brother to the park.» What does tagged along mean? | Pushed him on the swings | Ran away from him | *Went with him, often without being asked | Told him to stay at home
exam: «The old book was tagged with a name inside its cover, so everyone knew whose it was.» What does tagged mean here? | Was lost in the library | *Had a name label fixed to it | Was read by every class | Was locked in a cupboard
